{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06644b91-4fbe-599a-9474-1ebae7c48b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266199} {:answer/id #uuid "233d620a-e698-50bd-9389-aa9f5b7ca47c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266465} {:answer/id #uuid "3ddc55e6-09e8-59cd-8647-eda874503ae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266692} {:answer/id #uuid "e18ae79f-f50f-5f4c-a737-f0dd234b95b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268138} {:answer/id #uuid "e42c7b91-6155-5bf2-b915-b086395733d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266692} :answer-field/id #uuid "e40b29e1-b1eb-51b7-b542-712ddb83463b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268808}] :question/id #uuid "2faf3390-54b5-574c-8816-982dbf7402ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-13939" :question/problem "![](images/55/555cdb44522fab12ad67b54042ee4e47a085802df65c2b32a512eace16b92dd4.png)\n\nCalculate the area of the parallelogram in the figure." :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨1,2⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨2,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-5\\,|=5\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "186ee2ac-da11-5516-b903-e3b5e9480103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266346} {:answer/id #uuid "303f5039-136f-57c4-95b6-e45427ec1075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266570} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1f355e-f850-51c9-9c2a-fb7bc5bbb357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266684} {:answer/id #uuid "92a8e1d3-8eda-5c2f-9bb2-70ec28082ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267452} {:answer/id #uuid "a686bd68-cab0-5c69-85ea-bad821967fe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266570} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad50c151-5c0e-566c-ac0d-79838b4014d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268718}] :question/id #uuid "cad6730b-4b4a-5d91-acf2-b03ce7ce4d8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-13944" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7a70285258e584708a7296a2a008536dec9c97750b48e5fe0eb2f8cb7761bed1.png)\n\nCalculate the area of the parallelogram in the figure." :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨3,2⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨2,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-10\\,|=10\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d768a08-43a7-50f3-bc2c-9d0aec2d145d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266547} {:answer/id #uuid "49c440bd-ae95-5742-ba82-03be224e0b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266798} {:answer/id #uuid "650a0407-08e2-55ea-afa8-98afe8bbc506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267039} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1ac682-0ef5-54bf-9790-851d28380cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267230} {:answer/id #uuid "dba30746-1bcd-5e32-976d-2a26e890257c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266798} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0ea674a-8479-5833-a353-9cc54ecf9166" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268781}] :question/id #uuid "19e02ca3-a6f7-5909-838c-8df1ebb7ea40" :question/math-academy-id "q-13951" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\text{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3-5\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,23\\,|=23\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cd02af3-9a0c-5ac1-80bc-1a94c3cda463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267103} {:answer/id #uuid "99857b79-bba8-5e11-8d5b-9f8eca4bdc4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267532} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ef5443-4611-587c-adf8-f3e45a7a1b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267750} {:answer/id #uuid "de774392-670c-5a82-82bb-af1b9713659c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268109} {:answer/id #uuid "fdda59bb-ef2c-52d1-a08b-48c083a05eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267103} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ea4afd-09dd-54d7-aa86-07bc86565b04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268411}] :question/id #uuid "725abed1-dcc0-5071-8bbf-bf93146b75d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-13953" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\text{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,6\\,|=6\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce84160-5ec9-55ee-b547-a4aed4d425a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266542} {:answer/id #uuid "6157f8d3-2b30-5