389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236058} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d6b8ea-54a8-58e8-b6f4-45d73f4a2279" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237737}] :question/id #uuid "dadf2056-3a4c-505a-a071-2867e2e0c57e" :question/math-academy-id "q-102760" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\text{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =3-3 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "609f7b5f-824f-5147-9406-7af9613b62e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297963} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a79ff4-55ea-5211-91a9-33767972b15d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299294}] :question/id #uuid "53380aeb-e3ec-5770-a193-a3eec01995c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-320550" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=⟨\\frac{3}{2},-5⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨a,6⟩$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & a \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & a \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 6-a\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =9+5a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9+5a & =0 \\\\ 5a & =-9 \\\\ a & =-\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75dc16f3-b24c-59e8-aac9-c1ea4729e37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298066} :answer-field/id #uuid "70277a6d-54df-5d86-932e-e42ed6a7a735" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299017}] :question/id #uuid "6597267d-a0da-5d5e-b28e-9dd4c1c2688b" :question/math-academy-id "q-320553" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=⟨-\\frac{4}{3},7⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨a,-9⟩$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{3} & a \\\\ 7 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{4}{3} & a \\\\ 7 & -9\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{4}{3})\\cdot (-9)-a\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =12-7a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-7a & =0 \\\\ 7a & =12 \\\\ a & =\\frac{12}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e8c81fe-246e-57ca-a489-3e90a1b01ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298170} :answer-field/id #uuid "8766dc08-52b5-57f0-a29d-8b40f0a1ad6a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299091}] :question/id #uuid "2e91baa4-e2fe-58ac-ba3a-3b023f074435" :question/math-academy-id "q-320556" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=⟨3\\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{5}⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨a,\\,10⟩$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 10\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 10-a\\cdot (-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =30\\sqrt{2}+a\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30\\sqrt{2}+a\\sqrt{5} & =0 \\\\ a\\sqrt{5} & =-30\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ a & =-\\frac{30\\sqrt{10}}{5} \\\\ a & =-6\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72ba0de8-d856-579e-918d-924c542513ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298047} :answer-field/id #uuid "285ddb88-a48d-55de-a633-cf3747e9f898" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298771}] :question/id #uuid "53138b4d-25df-5dbe-9072-3708ca850fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-320557" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\text{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & a \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{2})\\cdot 6-a\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}-3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{2}-3a & =0 \\\\ -3a & =-12\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "511bc076-6388-527d-9ef2-97562ff289bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297892} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b1d6b1e-107a-52c6-beb0-de130a1ad00b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298786}] :question/id #uuid "fb3235d6-3da0-50ae-8be8-4a92d3030a44" :question/math-academy-id "q-320558" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\text{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{7} & a \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\sqrt{7} & a \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{7})(-10)-a\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{7}-5a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\sqrt{7}-5a & =0 \\\\ 5a & =10\\sqrt{7} \\\\ a & =2\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d979261-b00f-5b07-934f-d9becb3fb3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333109} {:answer/id #uuid "1c91238d-36cf-527e-8b6b-6cad045c8204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333246} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8bf08b-1cc2-59de-a1ba-777b195023cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334125} {:answer/id #uuid "82ae6838-8ddb-54d9-a045-f1a8ea096659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334155} {:answer/id #uuid "8737c0c8-20be-5d68-93e5-6d7c391191b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334125} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dcb8695-5ddf-5c8b-8e2f-29aa15a6844f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335294}] :question/id #uuid "7214ad71-6f54-5736-979a-1f4039dc6fdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-69938" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=⟨-2,3⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨4,-6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12-12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028cd858-4c44-5058-9e3c-4454de059b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333009} {:answer/id #uuid "290f684f-0aeb-5e5e-8b27-ced38ee80d5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333368} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff3a6bd-59f6-5889-aaa9-4b442955edfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333433} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e9c006-046a-59e8-91ab-82a5b68ea71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334855} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd21047-1a24-5ddc-9261-998eb3a209b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333368} :answer-field/id #uuid "991678fc-f88a-503b-ac76-3ea28edd13aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335525}] :question/id #uuid "6e1b0899-7688-507f-be9e-fc4727af5605" :question/math-academy-id "q-69940" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\text{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begi