 \\begin{bmatrix}1.1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nG = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 1.1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nH = \\begin{bmatrix}4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $F$ has $3$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 1.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $G$ has $1$ row and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $H$ has $1$ row and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 1.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $F$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "565541ca-26c6-521f-9fe8-23d37d60a9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476037} {:answer/id #uuid "ff82c4e9-cf50-526d-8ead-c45fbbb3c300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476100} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a19e31c-74ea-53be-97a0-90b84752832a" :answer-field/key "L" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0c9b9e6-088c-518b-b4ec-41929c745e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476072} {:answer/id #uuid "da854207-a539-5149-90f6-cff1baa64002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476083} :answer-field/id #uuid "af99871e-b845-516f-9c2f-5bb6c6c9bc80" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c9e3fb2-33ae-5af1-af4d-0fedf00a5617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476045} {:answer/id #uuid "fdae029a-4db3-5424-8935-e6e4ecbdde3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476098} :answer-field/id #uuid "de542c56-0134-522c-89d3-e885d88041d1" :answer-field/key "N" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476086}] :question/id #uuid "ee8835df-79c8-580f-8874-6ff83892351a" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $3\\times 3$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nL = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0 \\\\ 7 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nM = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -3 & -0.1 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nN = \\begin{bmatrix}1.1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1.1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $L$ has $3$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $M$ has $2$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $N$ has $3$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 3.$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, only $N$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f35ed92-67dc-5e42-b374-d0c7e8405853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476015} {:answer/id #uuid "bb419b41-076b-566f-ae1c-adbc9a7ffd06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476070} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f2e045a-dad7-5089-8346-f0284745230c" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007b3975-65a8-5413-b36a-b9448f221cd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476002} {:answer/id #uuid "8b080334-d984-5f31-a4fd-acc19f63cc8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476002} :answer-field/id #uuid "8548c722-2709-50df-a821-ba0277d85aab" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26023443-0660-5c5e-bbae-86d947803efc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476017} {:answer/id #uuid "26831adf-9ff0-53f0-bc31-e8bf1ad7ab85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476017} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc70ee49-90ab-56ac-a54f-3b376665a34b" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476078}] :question/id #uuid "f9fa0847-eb01-5dd2-be09-73c41b346b73" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $4\\times 3$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -0.1 \\\\ -0.1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -0.1 \\\\ -1 & 1.1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC = \\begin{bmatrix}1.1 & \\sqrt{2} & -0.1 \\\\ -2 & -0.1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ has $4$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $4$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 3.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476097 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dfbf4c9-b1c4-549c-80ea-2c3adecee66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476048} {:answer/id #uuid "b9fa25ad-4b66-5943-a3c9-f1dedb2d52c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476069} :answer-field/id #uuid "0296401d-1721-5e67-a2b7-c58a10f0590f" :answer-field/key "G" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476003} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff896a2-a7d2-5bb9-92f7-a599db8404a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476025} {:answer/id #uuid "43edb404-7674-5761-ab18-45c830f87ac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476028} :answer-field/id #uuid "42663f7a-38a4-5cc4-8f6a-efe7b6b220eb" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a27c788c-44c9-58c2-bd76-91c916f6370e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476063} {:answer/id #uuid "ac4b9116-661d-5172-abe3-c6f3a5913267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476063} :answer-field/id #uuid "dee260e6-6241-5c72-aa2d-ad4949f179bc" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476089}] :question/id #uuid "fb51fb5a-4174-5854-a7d1-95ace128827c" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $1\\times 2$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nE = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nF = \\begin{bmatrix}-0.1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nG = \\begin{bmatrix}1.1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $E$ has $1$ row and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 1.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $F$ has $2$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 1.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $G$ has $1$ row and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, only $G$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087819 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087654 :question/id #uuid "5c3b6d53-3dbb-59f6-8d15-a9e6f48927a1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9942" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9af4801abdec165de2b720a21dd6a727c578e32cbae9c9c54bd589a1b65043b0.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows train routes between three train stations, where the nodes represent stations and arrows represent the directed routes between them. The (incomplete) route matrix below represents the number of routes between the three stations. Find the value of $a+b+c.$\n\n<div class=\"route-matrix\">\n  <span class=\"matrix-to\">To</span>\n  <span class=\"matrix-from\">From</span>\n  <table aria-label=\"Route matrix: rows are From stations; columns are To stations\">\n    <thead>\n      <tr><td class=\"matrix-corner\"></td><th scope=\"col\">A</th><th scope=\"col\">B</th><th scope=\"col\">C</th></tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><th scope=\"row\">A</th><td>$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}a}$</td><td>$1$</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n      <tr><th scope=\"row\">B</th><td>$0$</td><td>$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}b}$</td><td>$2$</td></tr>\n      <tr><th scope=\"row\">C</th><td>$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}c}$</td><td>$0$</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our diagram.\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station A and ending at Station A. So, there is only one route from $A$ to $A,$ and so $a=1.$\n\n- No arrows are starting at Station B and ending at Station B. So, there are no routes from $B$ to $B,$ and so $b=0.$\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station C and ending at Station A. So, there is only one route from $C$ to $A,$ and so $c=1.$\n\nAs a result, our route matrix is the following:\n\n<div class=\"route-matrix\">\n  <span class=\"matrix-to\">To</span>\n  <span class=\"matrix-from\">From</span>\n  <table aria-label=\"Route matrix: rows are From stations; columns are To stations\">\n    <thead>\n      <tr><td class=\"matrix-corner\"></td><th scope=\"col\">A</th><th scope=\"col\">B</th><th scope=\"col\">C</th></tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><th scope=\"row\">A</th><td>$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td><td>$1$</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n      <tr><th scope=\"row\">B</th><td>$0$</td><td>$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$</td><td>$2$</td></tr>\n      <tr><th scope=\"row\">C</th><td>$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td><td>$0$</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+0+1 = 2.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10ca3efc-7d23-5bc1-ab41-f785bed69986" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476174 :question-generator/id #uuid "dfffdbe0-55bc-5179-afd6-8833cf35d3d2" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186087819.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088004 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c96a891-effe-5393-9122-2fd45c7880a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084759} {:answer/id #uuid "a56af5ae-6c68-5eec-9691-9f0c10aa2a51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084760} {:answe